#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1399
msgid "Conformance"
msgstr "Överensstämmelse"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1401
msgid ""
"This section describes the conformance requirements and relationships "
"between the Python DOM API, the W3C DOM recommendations, and the OMG IDL "
"mapping for Python."
msgstr ""
"I detta avsnitt beskrivs överensstämmelsekraven och relationerna mellan "
"Python DOM API, W3C DOM-rekommendationerna och OMG IDL-mappningen för Python."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1409
msgid "Type Mapping"
msgstr "Mappning av typ"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1411
msgid ""
"The IDL types used in the DOM specification are mapped to Python types "
"according to the following table."
msgstr ""
"De IDL-typer som används i DOM-specifikationen mappas till Python-typer "
"enligt följande tabell."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1415
msgid "IDL Type"
msgstr "IDL-typ"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1415
msgid "Python Type"
msgstr "Python Type"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1417
msgid "``boolean``"
msgstr "``boolean``"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1417
msgid "``bool`` or ``int``"
msgstr "``bool`` eller ``int``"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1419 ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1421
#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1423
msgid "``int``"
msgstr "``int``"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1421
msgid "``long int``"
msgstr "``long int``"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1423
msgid "``unsigned int``"
msgstr "``unsigned int``"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1425
msgid "``DOMString``"
msgstr "``DOMString``"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1425
msgid "``str`` or ``bytes``"
msgstr "``str`` eller ``bytes``"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1427
msgid "``null``"
msgstr "``null``"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1433
msgid "Accessor Methods"
msgstr "Accessor-metoder"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1435
msgid ""
"The mapping from OMG IDL to Python defines accessor functions for IDL "
"``attribute`` declarations in much the way the Java mapping does. Mapping "
"the IDL declarations ::"
msgstr ""
"Mappningen från OMG IDL till Python definierar accessorfunktioner för IDL "
"``attribut``\\-deklarationer på ungefär samma sätt som Java-mappningen gör. "
"Mappning av IDL-deklarationer ::"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1439
msgid ""
"readonly attribute string someValue;\n"
"         attribute string anotherValue;"
msgstr ""
"readonly attribut sträng someValue;\n"
"         attribut sträng anotherValue;"

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1442
msgid ""
"yields three accessor functions:  a \"get\" method for :attr:`!someValue` (:"
"meth:`!_get_someValue`), and \"get\" and \"set\" methods for :attr:`!"
"anotherValue` (:meth:`!_get_anotherValue` and :meth:`!_set_anotherValue`).  "
"The mapping, in particular, does not require that the IDL attributes are "
"accessible as normal Python attributes:  ``object.someValue`` is *not* "
"required to work, and may raise an :exc:`AttributeError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1449
msgid ""
"The Python DOM API, however, *does* require that normal attribute access "
"work. This means that the typical surrogates generated by Python IDL "
"compilers are not likely to work, and wrapper objects may be needed on the "
"client if the DOM objects are accessed via CORBA. While this does require "
"some additional consideration for CORBA DOM clients, the implementers with "
"experience using DOM over CORBA from Python do not consider this a problem.  "
"Attributes that are declared ``readonly`` may not restrict write access in "
"all DOM implementations."
msgstr ""
"Python DOM API *kräver* dock att normal attributåtkomst fungerar. Detta "
"innebär att de typiska surrogaten som genereras av Python IDL-kompilatorer "
"sannolikt inte kommer att fungera, och omslagsobjekt kan behövas på klienten "
"om DOM-objekten nås via CORBA. Även om detta kräver lite extra hänsyn för "
"CORBA DOM-klienter, anser implementatörerna med erfarenhet av att använda "
"DOM över CORBA från Python inte att detta är ett problem.  Attribut som "
"deklareras som ``readonly`` kanske inte begränsar skrivåtkomst i alla DOM-"
"implementeringar."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1458
msgid ""
"In the Python DOM API, accessor functions are not required.  If provided, "
"they should take the form defined by the Python IDL mapping, but these "
"methods are considered unnecessary since the attributes are accessible "
"directly from Python. \"Set\" accessors should never be provided for "
"``readonly`` attributes."
msgstr ""
"I Python DOM API krävs inte accessorfunktioner.  Om de tillhandahålls bör de "
"ha den form som definieras av Python IDL-mappningen, men dessa metoder anses "
"vara onödiga eftersom attributen är tillgängliga direkt från Python. \"Set\"-"
"accessorer bör aldrig tillhandahållas för ``readonly``\\-attribut."

#: ../../library/xml.dom.rst:1463
msgid ""
"The IDL definitions do not fully embody the requirements of the W3C DOM API, "
"such as the notion of certain objects, such as the return value of :meth:"
"`~Element.getElementsByTagName`, being \"live\".  The Python DOM API does "
"not require implementations to enforce such requirements."
msgstr ""
